Elysium is a citadel in the open [[Geography/index|Astra]], outside any sphere, kept by [[People/Althane/The Broker|Tech of Sedecium]]. It is sixteen castles of steel joined by bridges, standing where the suns of other spheres show as points of light in a black sky, and people in blue robes walk its halls. Bridges of light run between its towers, and a ring of water hangs about it for ornament.

At its main promenade stand four statues in the archways: a well-dressed merfolk wizard with staff and spellbook, an armored old knight, a tall cowlike being wreathed in flame, and the Broker itself, dark metal and wood holding a stack of books. The promenade is floored in tiny tiles, and up a shifting elevator lies the hall of the Keymaster, lined with books, scrolls and rolled canvases.

Elysium holds a weave of its own, raised by the Broker with a wizard's help and the aid of a [[Divinity/Higher Kind|higher kind]]. It is a place where travelers between spheres can rest while their bodies take the change, and a market where magic of every kind can be had, spells copied into books at a fraction of the usual work. No whole people can be brought into it: too many from one weave will raise that weave over the citadel's own and unravel both.
